    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31-a3">

                <pb facs="0054" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg47"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    31.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-02"><hi rendition="#small-caps">April</hi> 2,
                        1894</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Governor and
                        Comptroller</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San Juan del Norte:</hi></p>
                <p>With grief the executive power has been informed of the dangerous wound inflicted
                    on Mr. Wilson by an officer of that port, and through me, commands that you make
                    the courts proceed with all possible energy and activity in the repression of
                    that crime.</p>
                <p>The Minister of the Interior by the law,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Matus.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>This is a true copy. Managua, April 2, 1894.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. C. Matus.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
